'''Scarf Cat''' is a [[:Category:Special Cats|Special Cat]] that can be obtained from the [[Nyanko Rangers (Event Gacha)|Nyanko Rangers]] Event Gacha using Justice Hearts. It was added in [[Version 15.0 Update|Version 15.0]] for [[Nyanko Daisensou|BCJP]] and in [[Version 15.4 Update|Version 15.4]] for [[The Battle Cats|BCEN]].

{{Cat Info
|ID = 831
|rarity = EX
|name1 = Scarf Cat
|name2 = Red Nyanko Ranger
}}

==Evolution==
Evolves into '''Red Nyanko Ranger''' at level 10.

==Strategy/Usage==
This Cat moves fast and attacks fast, but is finicky to a fault. Red Nyanko Ranger is a middling anti-[[:Category:Aku Enemies|Aku]] DPS that performs well against shorter-ranged targets like [[Aku Gory]], [[Condemned Peng]], and [[Medu-san]]. The largest part of their survivability against Aku is gated behind [[Gold Silver Strike (Combo)|Gold Silver Strike]]'s Surge Immunity effect, which is essentially mandatory to run when using them against most Death Surge enemies, otherwise they tend to die to a light breeze. (The units required for this [[Cat Combo]] are currently exclusive to the Japanese version of The Battle Cats.) Red Nyanko Ranger sustains 8,400 Area-DPS against targets at Lv.50, which is actually quite decent, only being held back by their abysmally long recharge rate. However, this performance is usually not good enough to justify the opportunity cost of burning two valuable upper-row slots for an otherwise useless Cat Combo, all to bolster the matchups of one situationally useful cat. Red Nyanko Ranger can still be useful for midgame in [[The Aku Realms]], where dedicated Aku counters like them are uncommon enough to be worth considering even without Gold Silver Strike, but by lategame, [[Paperboy Cat (Rare Cat)|Paperboy Cat]] completely outclasses them in every regard.

Despite this, with [[Helmet Cat (Special Cat)|Helmet Cat]]'s Wave Immunity [[Cat Combo|Combo]], Red Nyanko Ranger can be used as a decently powerful soft-counter to [[Deathkory]]. But their own "Kaijin Slayer" Effect Combo lacks any purpose outside of the [[Anniversary/13th Year|only event]] where [[:Category:Kaijin Enemies|Kaijin Enemies]] appear, so this cat will generally not be considered for use when stacking Nyanko Ranger Combos.

In truth, Red Nyanko Ranger is usually not even worth considering for {{4c}} restriction stages either, outside of Deathkory, especially with just how powerful Paperboy Cat and [[Li'l Lizard Cat (Special Cat)|Li'l King Dragon Cat]] already are in this environment; by the time Aku are introduced in [[Legend Stages#Uncanny Legends|Uncanny Legend]] subchapters, the boat for any meaningful usage has long since sailed. This unit is best reserved for the [[Underground Labyrinth]].

